  The evaluation is based on nuclear model calculations that      8237 1451  129
have been benchmarked to experimental data, especially for n +    8237 1451  130
Pb and p + Pb208 reactions [Ch96a]. We use the GNASH code system  8237 1451  131
[Yo92], which utilizes Hauser-Feshbach statistical, preequi-      8237 1451  132
librium and direct-reaction theories. Coupled-channel and         8237 1451  133
spherical optical model calculations are used to obtain particle  8237 1451  134
transmission coefficients for the Hauser-Feshbach calculations,   8237 1451  135
as well as for the elastic neutron angular distributions.         8237 1451  136
  Cross sections and spectra for producing individual residual    8237 1451  137
nuclei are included for reactions that exceed a cross section of  8237 1451  138
approximately 1 nb at any energy. The energy-angle-correlations   8237 1451  139
for all outgoing particles are based on Kalbach systematics       8237 1451  140
[Ka88].                                                           8237 1451  141
  A model was developed to calculate the energy distributions of  8237 1451  142
all recoil nuclei in the GNASH calculations [Ch96b]. The recoil   8237 1451  143
energy distributions are represented in the laboratory system in  8237 1451  144
MT=5, MF=6, and are given as isotropic in the lab system. Note    8237 1451  145
that all other data in MT=5,MF=6 are given in the center-of-mass  8237 1451  146
system. This method of representation requires a modification of  8237 1451  147
the original ENDF-6 format.                                       8237 1451  148
  Preequilibrium corrections were performed in the course of the  8237 1451  149
