 Changes for current evaluation:                                  8237 1451  494
  1. Isotopic evaluation is now given for 206,207,208Pb.          8237 1451  495
  2. Resonance parameters were introduced [LA89,HO86].            8237 1451  496
  3. Energy-angle correlated spectra of secondary neutrons are    8237 1451  497
     given for the first time.                                    8237 1451  498
  4. Gamma-ray production spectra are now given for each reaction 8237 1451  499
     and each isotope.                                            8237 1451  500
  5. Recoil spectra are given to enable precise energy balance    8237 1451  501
     checks.                                                      8237 1451  502
  6. Gamma-ray transition probabilities are given for the         8237 1451  503
     discrete inelastic levels for perfect energy balance.        8237 1451  504
  7. Gamma-ray spectra from capture are based on calculations     8237 1451  505
     using experimental primary transition probabilities and      8237 1451  506
     branching ratios.  This removes energy-balance problems in   8237 1451  507
     the natural evaluation as the q values for the various       8237 1451  508
     isotopes differ significantly.                               8237 1451  509
  8. The precompound-strength, collective-strength, and level-    8237 1451  510
     density parameters were fine-tuned to accomodate new data    8237 1451  511
     for (n,2n) cross sections [FR80,IW88,TA86] and neutron       8237 1451  512
     emission spectra [PA88,TA86].                                8237 1451  513
